{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":150848,"name":"","username":"jujujampada","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.ghost.org/jujujampada/{size}/41187_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-29T14:27:02.668Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAbout the project\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA curated literature project, organised around thematic keywords, for international English-reading audiences. The site runs on Ghost CMS with a two-tier membership model:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFree tier\u003c/strong\u003e: reviews, previews, and promotional content\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaid tier\u003c/strong\u003e (~€2/month or €17/year): interviews, paratext, archive access, and discounted access to publications\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlongside the membership content, we’re launching a translation series of standalone e-books (starting with works on bodies, gender, and political theory) sold directly from the same Ghost site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-150848-what-we-need-built-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-150848-what-we-need-built-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat we need built\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eE-book storefront on Ghost\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEmbed a checkout/buy-button system (e.g. Payhip or Snipcart) into individual Ghost book pages via code injection, keeping the storefront visually native to the site rather than redirecting to a third-party page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEach book has its own page with consistent presentation for all visitors (subscribers and non-subscribers see the same layout).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFree-for-subscribers, paid-for-everyone-else pricing\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNon-subscribers pay full price per book through the embedded checkout.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePaid subscribers get the book for free via a discount/coupon code (100% off), accessible only on a members-only Ghost page.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIdeally, codes can be rotated periodically (e.g. monthly) to reduce sharing/leakage, without requiring manual reconfiguration each time.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDelivery integration\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConnect checkout (Payhip or equivalent) to BookFunnel via webhook so buyers/subscribers automatically receive a properly formatted e-book file (EPUB/MOBI/PDF) after purchase or code redemption.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGhost membership tier setup\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfigure Ghost’s native membership/content gating for the free vs. paid tiers described above.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet up member-only content blocks (e.g. the discount codes page) visible only to logged-in paid subscribers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-150848-ideal-experience-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-150848-ideal-experience-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIdeal experience\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrior hands-on work with \u003cstrong\u003eGhost CMS\u003c/strong\u003e (themes, Handlebars templating, code injection, membership/Portal configuration)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExperience integrating \u003cstrong\u003ePayhip, Snipcart, or similar checkout tools\u003c/strong\u003e into a non-Shopify/WooCommerce site\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBonus: familiarity with \u003cstrong\u003eBookFunnel\u003c/strong\u003e or similar e-book delivery services\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-150848-engagement-structure-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-150848-engagement-structure-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEngagement structure\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe’re looking for an ongoing collaborator rather than a one-off contractor – proposing a \u003cstrong\u003esmall monthly retainer plus performance-based bonuses\u003c/strong\u003e tied to launch milestones and subscriber growth. Open to discussing structure with the right person.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-150848-to-apply-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-150848-to-apply-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTo apply\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease share:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e*** Examples of past Ghost CMS projects (theme customisation, integrations, or membership setups)**\u003cbr\u003e\n*** Your general approach to combining a subscription model with one-off product sales**\u003cbr\u003e\n*** Availability and preferred engagement structure (retainer, hourly, or hybrid)**\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-07-29T14:27:13.267Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":18,"reads":18,"readers_count":17,"score":93.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":63458,"topic_slug":"developer-wanted-ghost-cms-integration-for-a-literary-subscription-site","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":27975,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/developer-wanted-ghost-cms-integration-for-a-literary-subscription-site/63458/1","calendar_details":[],"reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":150851,"name":"Cathy Sarisky (Spectral Web Services)","username":"Cathy_Sarisky","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.ghost.org/cathy_sarisky/{size}/25750_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-29T14:50:52.472Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThere’s not much here that’s actually Ghost work.  There’s some basic config that can be done in the Ghost dashboard and post editor (i.e. set up tiers, mark content as paid members only).  You could hire that out, but you might very well not need to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut really, you need to decide on a checkout platform, and then drop its embed code onto your site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI did a snipcart \u0026amp; ghost demo a while back, here. It’s not too bad to do – what you’re looking at is all code injection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://www.spectralwebservices.com/blog/snipcart-and-ghost-integration/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex015/uploads/ghost2/original/3X/5/c/5c0d3f1c1987d3ee7ed656478dcd15d9bc10b2bb.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"AC70AA\" width=\"180\" height=\"180\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://www.spectralwebservices.com/blog/snipcart-and-ghost-integration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"04:51AM - 12 February 2025\"\u003eSpectral Web Services – 12 Feb 25\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:620/400;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex015/uploads/ghost2/original/3X/5/3/53778d41b8ad3c81fe9768ff2b3b420a57db6568.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"E8D47C\" width=\"620\" height=\"400\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.spectralwebservices.com/blog/snipcart-and-ghost-integration/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eA Snipcart test\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eDoes Snipcart work with Ghost?  I tried it out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThere’s also an actual official doc on how to do it:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://ghost.org/integrations/snipcart/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://ghost.org/integrations/snipcart/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eGhost - The Professional Publishing Platform\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/344;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://ghost.org/images/meta/ghost-integrations.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" width=\"690\" height=\"356\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://ghost.org/integrations/snipcart/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eOfficial Ghost + Snipcart Integration\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eUse Snipcart to turn your Ghost publication into a fully customisable ecommerce platform and start selling products directly to your readers 💰\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eand, I assume you’ve found the Ghost Experts directory, right? \u003ca href=\"https://ghost.org/experts/\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGhost Experts\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m on that list, but I’m not interested in a bonus-based compensation plan. :)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-07-29T14:50:52.472Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":16,"readers_count":15,"score":23.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":63458,"topic_slug":"developer-wanted-ghost-cms-integration-for-a-literary-subscription-site","display_username":"Cathy Sarisky (Spectral Web Services)","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://ghost.org/experts/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Ghost Experts","clicks":1},{"url":"https://www.spectralwebservices.com/blog/snipcart-and-ghost-integration/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"A Snipcart test - Spectral Web Services","clicks":1},{"url":"https://ghost.org/integrations/snipcart/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Official Ghost + Snipcart Integration","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":12499,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/developer-wanted-ghost-cms-integration-for-a-literary-subscription-site/63458/2","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[150848,150851]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,102]],"sugges